    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is anchored by the elite offensive profile of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who boasts an 86.63 score against Hughes. His outlook is bolstered significantly by favorable park factors and wind patterns shifting out, making him our highest-upside play for counting stats. **Bryce Harper** (76.31) also projects as a must-start; despite a matchup against the left-handed Mathews, his high xwOBA and top-third batting order placement mitigate the platoon disadvantage, making him our primary engine for RBI production. We are also leaning heavily into **Lawrence Butler** (69.13) and **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) today, as both benefit from advantageous matchups against right-handed pitching, providing the necessary volume to keep pace in our 5x5 targets.\n\nWhile the core is set, we are monitoring two key risks. **Jonathan Aranda**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** are all playing in environments with a roughly 40-45% rain risk, which could truncate their plate appearances and force us to rely on our deeper bench. Regarding our roster construction, **Gavin Sheets** (46.97) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine. While his platoon splits against Kremer are positive, his limited upside compared to the established floor of **Daulton Varsho** (54.55) or **Zack Gelof** (55.93) kept him sidelined to preserve game caps. We are also wary of the matchup for **Gleyber Torres** (47.73), whose negative platoon splits and poor BvP history against Wacha make him our most fragile start, though we currently lack a superior option to replace his production profile at 2B today.",
